Quickly fixing negatively enchanted armor is a good use for it, but
that is most useful only in the very early game when you haven't had a
chance to acquire some better stuff.  Valks getting their ascension
kits ready might like to maximize the enchantment of Mjollnir.  Well,
if you enchant Mojo up to +3 and read a blessed scroll of enchant
weapon hoping for +5 but wind up with +4 instead, you can't simply
engrave back down to +3 to try again since blunt weapons only write in
the dust.  But you can cancel it back to +0 quite easily and try again
if you have the scrolls to burn.

